@prefix chg: <https://semblance.dev/ns/change#> .
@prefix mig: <https://semblance.dev/ns/migration#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix change: <https://semblance.dev/change/> .
@prefix c: <https://semblance.dev/ns/component#> .
@prefix sem: <https://semblance.dev/ns/core#> .

# What changed for whoever has to move with it: AGENTS.md, "When a component changes".

change:search-field-disabled a chg:Change ;
    rdfs:label "A search field honours c:disabled"@en ;
    chg:issue <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/183> ;
    chg:motivation """A search field said nothing of c:disabled: while an index was loading, or a filter did not
apply, the field stayed editable and typing, the clear button and Escape still wrote to the controlled node, as
c:Choice, c:TextField and the other inputs do not.""" ;
    chg:substance """A c:SearchField with c:disabled true renders its input and its clear button with the disabled
attribute, and its reactions (typing, the clear button, Escape) write nothing while it is disabled; removing
c:disabled makes it usable again with what the controlled node holds. A disabled field is dimmed (opacity 0.55)
with a not-allowed cursor. A field without c:disabled renders and behaves as before.""" ;
    chg:forwardGuide """Nothing to move. A field that was disabled by other means (hidden, or a reaction that undid
its writes) can say c:disabled true instead.""" ;
    chg:backwardGuide """Nothing to move in the graph. Going back, c:disabled on a search field is ignored again: the
field is editable and writes.""" ;
    chg:affects c:SearchField .
